WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.270
Film Courage: So you’ve worked with a lot
of young students and I’m curious what the

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:08.830
idea in their minds about what it’s like
out there in the real world versus what the

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:13.099
real world really is in terms of …[considering]
whether they were the two best writers in

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:14.099
the whole class?

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:20.550
Corey Mandell: Well when I teach a class at
UCLA or my private workshops there are all

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:25.760
these people that just want to be professional
and they have no idea what it’s like to

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.689
be a professional writer and I don’t think
you ever know until you do it.

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:34.340
And so it’s just “I want to be a professional
writer and I have a vision of what that would

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:35.340
be.”

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.931
Most people’s vision is I sit in a room
(or in a room with other people) but let’s

00:00:40.931 --> 00:00:46.620
say I sit in a room and I write what I want
to write and I write it in a way that I want

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.100
to write it and I write what I love and everyone
else will love it.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.030
It don’t work that way.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.260
People have a process to how they write.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.870
And that process is usually what is comfortable
because it plays to their strengths and hides

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:00.870
their weaknesses.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.710
And it’s learning how to write in a way
that other people love it as much as you love

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:05.710
it.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:06.710
It takes a lot of work and training.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:10.491
And then there’s deadlines and there is
politics.

00:01:10.491 --> 00:01:14.810
There’s a lot that goes into having a writing
career beyond just the writing.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:18.829
I mean the reality was like you have two careers.

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:20.560
You have the writing, you have to create the
content.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.630
But then there’s the career management and
the meetings and the marketing and the always

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:26.799
be looking for your other job.

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:28.310
There’s a lot that goes into it.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:37.170
But at the same time, I mean to get paid and
to be able to make a living playing with characters

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:42.100
and playing with stories and doing something
that especially if it’s creatively fulfilling

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.090
and you get paid for it?

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:49.720
For people who do it right and train themselves
the right way, they literally do something

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:54.369
that they would do for free and they get paid
and perhaps they get paid millions of dollars.

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:56.060
Perhaps they get paid tens of millions of
dollars.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:57.639
Perhaps they get paid hundreds of thousands
of dollars.

00:01:57.639 --> 00:02:02.679
Perhaps they get paid 100 thousand dollars
to do what you would do for free?

00:02:02.679 --> 00:02:07.840
That actually is possible and I have a growing
list of clients and students who have that

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:08.840
lifestyle.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:16.110
So I think anyone who really is drawn to this
should absolutely pursue it and just pursue

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.800
it in the right ways.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:22.280
Film Courage: Can we talk about thought the
beginning stages of their career where a lot

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:27.320
of it is going to rest on discipline and being
your own taskmaster and it’s easy when you

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.920
think “Okay, I have to get back to this
person’s email about this or that once I

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.450
have something finished.”

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:35.360
But when in the beginning there is going to
be a lot of time alone.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.140
There is going to be a lot of time being your
own taskmaster, attempting to make something

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.140
and how difficult this is.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.220
Corey Mandell: Yeah so it’s really difficult
in the beginning and lot of writers have this

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:49.710
fantasy or this illusion (and I did and I
was wrong) is that you’re working and you’re

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:54.060
making money and you’re trying to write
and you’re so busy and writing so hard and

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.700
gosh, when you sell something and when you
get hired, you can quit your day job and you

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.580
can quit this and you can just write…Oh,
what a luxury that would be because you are

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:11.360
so time starved but when I first broke into
the business I had two months to write the

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.470
script to METROPOLIS but almost every day
I had meetings and I had to go in meetings

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:22.010
and I was talking to people about other projects
and pitching and I actually was spending more

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.190
time on that than I was on my day job.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:26.990
So I actually had less time to write.

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:31.460
You were just pulled in so many directions
and so discipline really matters.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:36.450
One of the things that I teach writers from
the very beginning, non-writers who are starting

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:42.120
out and then a lot of them wont do this but
the ones that do, not only do they become

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:48.310
better writers, this will save their rear-ends
when they have a career, is I teach them the

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.360
idea of a writer’s schedule.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:55.871
What that means is if you have a job that
pays the bills and Thursday at 3:00 p.m. you

00:03:55.871 --> 00:03:57.930
have to do a marketing proposal to your boss.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.930
I know where you’re going to be on Thursday
at 3:00 p.m.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:01.130
You’re going to be doing that proposal.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:04.490
If you don’t feel like it and you don’t
feel like the proposal is that good, you’re

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:06.210
still going to do the best you can.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:10.480
And if you feel like watching TV or napping,
you’re going to be there or you are not

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:16.010
going to have a job and from 10:00 a.m. to
12:00 p.m. you are supposed to meet with this

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:17.500
client, you’re going to do that.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.160
And you schedule your life around that.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:26.430
So what I tell people is no one is going to
treat you like a professional until you are

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:27.430
a professional.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:32.500
No one is going to invest money in you until
you put your money where your mouth is.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.250
So you have a career.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.500
Perhaps you have a family.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.320
Perhaps you have all of these pulls on your
time (I get that).

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.530
Every Sunday night you are going to create
a writer’s schedule for the next week.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:46.890
And maybe you can only write 45 minutes a
day, ideally an hour or two hours.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.490
Let’s say 90 minutes a day.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:54.810
You will block out that writing time, be it
at 7:30 in the morning, be it at 6:00 p.m.,

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.180
whatever it is for every day at that week.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:03.500
Now if you’ve blocked out Thursday from
7:30 to 8:30 is your writing time, I know

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:04.590
where you are going to be at 7:30.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.350
You are going to be writing.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:08.170
And it’s not like if you feel like it.

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:10.820
Because that’s like your marketing meeting
with your boss.

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:16.370
So you schedule out your writing time every
single week and then you honor that.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:20.240
And if you’re not willing to do that and
you’re not willing to honor that, why should

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:22.650
anyone else invest money in you?

